{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 21, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Wronskian matrix of sin(x), cos(x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)\n  [ sin(x)   cos(x)  ]   the functions\n  [ cos(x)   -sin(x) ]   d/dx\n  W = det = -1\n  (W equals the numeric determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 3e-15)\n  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = -1 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 21, "ok": true, "cmd": "wronskian", "ucas": "wronskian sin(x), cos(x) wrt x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "wronskian", "var": "x", "matrix": [["sin(x)", "cos(x)"], ["cos(x)", "-sin(x)"]], "wronskian": "-1", "independent": true, "witness_x": -0.05000000000000071, "witness_w": -1}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 402, "max_diff": 2.896608734120898e-15, "passed": true}], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "W != 0 at a sample point"}, "files": [], "text": "Wronskian matrix of sin(x), cos(x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)\n  [ sin(x)   cos(x)  ]   the functions\n  [ cos(x)   -sin(x) ]   d/dx\n  W = det = -1\n  (W equals the numeric determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 3e-15)\n  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = -1 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 22, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:\n  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)\n  = 1 (from both sides)\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 22, "ok": true, "cmd": "limit", "ucas": "limit sin(x)/x as x -> (0)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "limit", "var": "x", "at": "0", "side": "both", "limit": {"kind": "number", "value": 1, "text": "1"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "numeric_left", "points": 22, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "Richardson-extrapolated values approaching the point"}, {"kind": "numeric_right", "points": 22, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "Richardson-extrapolated values approaching the point"}], "files": [], "text": "limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:\n  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)\n  = 1 (from both sides)\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 23, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Maclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of sin(x) at x = 0, through order 5:\n  sin(x) = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 + O(x^6)\n  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 0 1 0 -1/6 0 1/120\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 1.98e-11 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 1.55e-13 at ± 1/20, 1.21e-15 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^7.0; expected >= 6)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 23, "ok": true, "cmd": "taylor", "ucas": "taylor sin(x) x at 0 order 5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "taylor", "var": "x", "at": 0, "order": 5, "polynomial": "x - x^3/6 + x^5/120", "coefficients": ["0", "1", "0", "-1/6", "0", "1/120"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "taylor_jet", "points": 6, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "coefficients against long double Taylor-jet arithmetic"}], "files": [], "text": "Maclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of sin(x) at x = 0, through order 5:\n  sin(x) = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 + O(x^6)\n  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 0 1 0 -1/6 0 1/120\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 1.98e-11 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 1.55e-13 at ± 1/20, 1.21e-15 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^7.0; expected >= 6)\n"}, "isError": false}}
